{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they shall measure.</b> Even if it is found conclusively, it is a commandment to engage in measuring, for through their involvement in the matter people will come from the measured cities, and whoever left his home and did not return — his family members come and identify the slain. If they recognize him, they testify about him, so that his wife will not be an agunah and his sons will take possession of their father's inheritance, and the court does not restrain them. And through this it will become known who went with him and who associated with him, and sometimes it is publicized through this."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:31.324558717Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}